1. The provider refuses connections

  POST /ask -> 503 (the model provider is not answering) after 0.5s

2. The provider accepts connections and never answers

  at 3s, with 8 requests waiting, a new one: POST /ask -> 503 (busy) after 0.0s
  the 8 held requests ended between 10s and 11s: 8 x 503
  then a new request: POST /ask ->
    503 (the model provider is not answering) after 10.5s

Before: a caller could wait 30 minutes, and a full bulkhead stayed full as long.
After: nobody waits longer than about 11s, the slots come back on
their own, and every caller is told the truth, with a Retry-After, instead of a
500 or a hang.
